course: dictionary
lesson: 12720
title: Downsize, and the soft words we use
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Downsize is a verb, so it is a doing word. Its forms are downsize, downsizes, downsized and downsizing. It means to make something smaller, often to save money. The context tells you which kind of smaller. «The company had to downsize after it lost its biggest customer.» Here a company is cutting its number of workers.
explain: Downsize can also be about a home. «When the children left, Gran and Grandad decided to downsize to a small flat.» Nobody is cutting workers here. They are moving to a smaller place, probably because it is cheaper and easier to look after.
explain: Sometimes people use downsize as a soft way to say something hard. «We are downsizing,» said the boss, and the room went quiet. Here the words may mean people are going to lose their jobs. Listen to the context and to how people feel when they hear the word.
fact: Downsize is a verb: downsize, downsizes, downsized, downsizing.
fact: «Downsize» means to make something smaller, often to save money.
fact: In business, «downsize the staff» means cutting the number of workers.
fact: In family life, «downsize to a flat» means moving to a smaller home.
fact: A euphemism is a gentle word used instead of a harsh one, and «We are downsizing» can hide the news that people are losing their jobs.
exercise: «When the children left, Gran and Grandad decided to downsize to a flat.» What does downsize mean here? | *To move to a smaller home | To go on a long holiday | To build an extra room | To buy a bigger car
exercise: «The company had to downsize after it lost its biggest customer.» What does the company do? | Makes its shop windows bigger | Grows very quickly | *Cuts its size, often by reducing the number of workers | Moves to the seaside
exercise: Ben's mum says, «We are downsizing,» and Ben feels worried. Why might he feel worried? | Because it is a sunny day | Because it means a holiday is coming | *Because it might mean people are losing their jobs | Because downsizing means getting a puppy
test: What is the past tense of downsize? | downsize | *downsized | downsizing | downsizes
test: A family moves into a smaller flat to save money. What are they doing? | Growing their house | Painting the walls | *Downsizing | Going camping
exam: Which sentence uses downsize in the same way as «The company had to downsize its staff»? | The boy grew three inches taller over the summer | The river flowed quickly into the sea | *The firm cut its workers to save money | The family bought a large new house by the lake
